sdata> -- REPL-mode companion to if_single_line_trailing_comma.cmd: the trailing
sdata> -- comma still triggers the "..>" continuation prompt (design.md sec5.4
sdata> -- applies unconditionally), even though the resulting merged statement then
sdata> -- fails for the same, separate, expected reason (ELSEIF cannot follow a
sdata> -- single-line IF).
sdata> LET inlrn=1
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> if inlrn then let sample$="Learn",
..>   elseif 0 then let sample$="Test"
Error: Unrecognized command "elseif" at line  2 — type HELP for a list of commands
sdata> run
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> quit
